---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { hrefWithBase } from '../lib/base';
import version from '../../version.json';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Nav Edge · HCI Nerdz"
  description="Two Nav Edge variants: Map Edge (wireframe directory) and Modal Edge (View Transitions ancestry stack)."
>
  <main class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">HCI Nerdz · MVP</p>
    <h1>Nav Edge</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Ecosystem navigation lives on the edge — not stuffed into the content header. Two variants
      help compare the idea: a <strong>Map Edge</strong> that summons a wireframe directory, a
      <strong>Modal Edge</strong> that slides the current sheet to reveal colored ancestor layers
      (windows on windows), and a <strong>Path Edge</strong> whose L-edge is a path trace — unique
      colors for the hops you took. Published docs still use “context rails” for the map-shaped claim.
    </p>
    <p class="meta-row">
      <a href="https://hci-nerdz.github.io/blog/when-platforms-overload-the-entrypoint/">Essay</a>
      <a href="https://hci-nerdz.github.io/docs/hci-nerdz/context-rails.html">Docs</a>
      <a href="https://hci-nerdz.github.io/demos/context-rails/">Site desk</a>
      <span>v{version.version}</span>
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.15rem;margin:1.5rem 0 0.65rem">
      Variant A · Map Edge
    </h2>
    <p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:42rem;line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 0.85rem">
      Click the edge → the activity page slides off (View Transitions) and a scrollable
      Alphabet/Google product tree is already underneath. Pick a node to enter that building.
    </p>
    <div class="demo-grid">
      <a class="demo-card" href={hrefWithBase('demos/solid-cloud/')}>
        <strong>Solid · cloud</strong>
        <span>Console parody with overload toggle and signal-driven rails.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="demo-card" href={hrefWithBase('demos/react-suite/')}>
        <strong>React · suite</strong>
        <span>Microsoft-suite-ish shell with duo-tone overlays (Next-portable).</span>
      </a>
      <a class="demo-card" href={hrefWithBase('demos/svelte-community/')}>
        <strong>Svelte · community</strong>
        <span>Reddit/SO-ish spaces with softer transitions.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="demo-card" href={hrefWithBase('demos/vanilla-mature/')}>
        <strong>Vanilla</strong>
        <span>Hover expands the L-edge; click slides this page off the map underneath.</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.15rem;margin:0.5rem 0 0.65rem">
      Variant B · Modal Edge
    </h2>
    <p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:42rem;line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 0.85rem">
      The edge <em>is</em> the current node. Click → View Transitions slide the sheet down and
      right; ancestor contexts remain as colored layers underneath. Click a layer to jump to that
      node. Also called Context Edge / Nav Edge in conversation.
    </p>
    <div class="demo-grid">
      <a class="demo-card" href={hrefWithBase('demos/modal-edge/')}>
        <strong>Modal Edge · Rest</strong>
        <span>Ancestry layers with slide-to-reveal (View Transitions API).</span>
      </a>
      <a class="demo-card" href={hrefWithBase('demos/modal-edge-live/')}>
        <strong>Modal Edge · Live</strong>
        <span>Pointer near the edge peeks the sheet.</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.15rem;margin:0.5rem 0 0.65rem">
      Variant C · Path Edge
    </h2>
    <p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:42rem;line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 0.85rem">
      The L-edge is a path trace: unique colors for the hops from root to here. Hover either
      edge and both present. Labels only on the top. One workshop: Color / Subtle, then Live /
      Live Subtle.
    </p>
    <div class="demo-grid">
      <a class="demo-card" href={hrefWithBase('demos/path-edge/')}>
        <strong>Path Edge</strong>
        <span>Color, Tint, Live, Live Tint — overflow-only compression, left pack origin.</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.15rem;margin:0 0 0.5rem">
      Framework impedance (short)
    </h2>
    <ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55;max-width:42rem;padding-left:1.2rem">
      <li>
        <strong style="color:var(--ink)">Solid / SolidStart</strong> — shines for long-lived shell
        state; drop the Solid island into a SolidStart layout (no SolidStart app required here).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong style="color:var(--ink)">React / Next.js</strong> — same shell as a
        <code>"use client"</code> layout wrapper; keep overlay identity in client state. Modal Edge
        pairs well with the View Transitions API in supporting browsers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong style="color:var(--ink)">Svelte / SvelteKit</strong> — strong for edge motion; Kit
        layouts mirror the substrate slot.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong style="color:var(--ink)">Astro islands</strong> — ideal for multi-framework demos;
        production SPAs should own rails inside their shell.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
